          <div>
    <div id="block-echo-page-title">
  
    
      
  <h1>
<span property="schema:name">Data Downloads</span>
</h1>


  </div>
<div id="block-echo-echo-system-main">
  
    
      <article data-history-node-id="113" about="/tools/data-downloads" typeof="schema:WebPage">

  
      <span property="schema:name" content="Data Downloads" class="hidden"></span>


  
  <div>
    
            <div property="schema:text"><p>The ECHO website with its <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/facilities/facility-search?mediaSelected=all" target="_blank">facility search</a> features is designed to provide easy access to EPA's compliance and enforcement data with customizable onscreen display and download (learn about facility searching in a <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/help/tutorials" target="_blank">video tutorial</a>). For those with larger data needs, ECHO has several types of datasets available. These large datasets may be of particular use to developers, programmers, academics, and analysts. The data available here can be downloaded and used for many different functions and are certain to meet all data retrieval needs.</p><ul><li><a href="#exporter">ECHO Exporter</a> - one line of data per facility</li><li><a href="#downloads">ECHO Data Downloads</a> - large sets of national data by data system<ul><li><a href="#FRS">Facility Registry Service (FRS) Download</a></li><li><a href="#community">Community and Demographic Downloads</a></li><li><a href="#tribal">Facility and Tribal Spatial Association Data Download</a></li><li><a href="#air">Air Stationary Source Data Downloads</a></li><li><a href="#NPDES">Water National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System (NPDES) Data Downloads</a></li><li><a href="#MSGP">Industrial Stormwater - Multi-Sector General Permit (MSGP)</a></li><li><a href="#biosolids">Water Biosolids Data Download</a></li><li><a href="#seweroverflow">Sewer Overflow Data Downloads</a></li><li><a href="#hazardouswaste">Hazardous Waste Data Download</a></li><li><a href="#ECM">EPA Enforcement and Compliance Monitoring Data Download</a></li><li><a href="#drinkingwater">Drinking Water Data Downloads</a></li><li><a href="#WQI">Water Quality Indicators (WQI) Data Download</a></li><li><a href="#PFAS">National PFAS Data Downloads</a></li></ul></li></ul><p>ECHO also offers:</p><ul><li><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/web-services" target="_blank">Web services</a>&nbsp;and <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/map-service" target="_blank">map services</a>&nbsp;to facilitate direct access to ECHO data by third-party applications</li><li><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/quick-search-widget" target="_blank">ECHO widget</a>&nbsp;to allow simple facility searching from your website</li><li>A variety of customizable, water pollutant-related datasets on the <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/trends/loading-tool/get-data" target="_blank">Water Pollutant Loading Tool</a> Data Downloads tab.</li></ul><p>Please note that each level of government has been working together for many years to ensure that information in national systems is accurate. However, while increased scrutiny has been given to the quality of data in the national systems in recent years, the data quality before November 2000 has not been assessed and should be considered unknown. For information about ECHO data sources and refresh schedules, please visit the <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/resources/echo-data/about-the-data" target="_blank">About the Data</a> page.</p><hr><h2>ECHO Exporter Version 2.0&nbsp;<a id="exporter" name="exporter">&nbsp;</a></h2><p>The ECHO Exporter draws from one of ECHO's most popular reports - providing summary information about each facility in a table format. Because ECHO has a limit on the number of facilities that can be shown in one query, some users were not able to get all the information they needed. The ECHO Exporter solves that problem - providing a download for more than 1.5 million regulated facilities in one zip file. Over 130 data fields are available for each facility, including the frequency of inspections, violations, actions, and penalties.</p><p>The file includes facilities regulated as Clean Air Act stationary sources, Clean Water Act direct dischargers, Resource Conservation and Recovery Act hazardous waste handlers, Safe Drinking Water Act public water systems along with other data, such as Toxics Release Inventory releases, industry codes, and permit types. Latitude/longitude information also is included when available, allowing users to integrate facility locations into maps, mobile apps, and websites. The FRS ID joins the data to other ECHO download files. To join Exporter data with other datasets, use the <a href="#FRS">FRS program interest linkages download</a>.</p><p>The ECHO Exporter download file is updated weekly as part of the ECHO <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/resources/echo-data/about-the-data#sources" target="_blank">data refresh</a>. <em>Note: this file is too large to work well in Excel. Microsoft Access, other database products like MySQL or APEX, and most GIS software can handle the data.</em></p><ul><li><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/echo_exporter.zip">ECHO Exporter (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(392 MB)</span></li><li><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/system/files/echo_exporter_columns_7-16-2025_0.xlsx">ECHO Exporter Summary file (XLSX)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(27K)</span></li></ul><hr><h2>National Enforcement and Compliance History Online Data Downloads&nbsp;<a id="downloads" name="downloads">&nbsp;</a></h2><p>The Enforcement and Compliance History Online (ECHO) datasets have been compiled for access to larger sets of national data to ensure that ECHO meets your data retrieval needs. While ECHO provides data detailing compliance assurance and enforcement activities related to federal environmental laws, it has a limited online display of data. The ECHO datasets are available for download to review these expanded datasets. Each dataset is a compressed zip file containing one or more comma-delimited text files. The download summary documents posted after each dataset contain a file listing and definitions of included data elements.</p><p>The datasets below are updated weekly as part of the ECHO <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/resources/echo-data/about-the-data#sources" target="_blank">data refresh</a>.&nbsp;<em>Note: as creation of these files is automated, the ZIP file sizes below are approximate. Some of the files may be too large to work well in Excel. Microsoft Access, other database products like MySQL or APEX, and most GIS software can handle the data.</em></p><h3 id="FRS">Facility Registry Service (FRS) Download</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/frs_downloads.zip" id="FRS" name="FRS">FRS Facilities and Linkages (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(318 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/frs-download-summary" target="_blank">FRS Download Summary</a></td><td>Facility identification data from EPA's Facility Registry Service (FRS), which integrates facility information from various EPA and state data systems.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="community">Community and Demographic Downloads</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/echo_demographics.zip" id="FRS" name="FRS">ECHO Facility Demographics (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(567 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/demographic-download-summary" target="_blank">ECHO Facility Demographics Download Summary</a></td><td>Demographic data describing the population within 1, 3, and 5 mile radii around the location of each facility in ECHO. This dataset is spatially derived from American Community Survey demographic data. The information is also presented for each facility on the Detailed Facility Report.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="tribal">Facility and Tribal Spatial Association Data Download</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/facility_tribal_spatial.zip" id="tribal" name="tribal">Facility and Tribal Spatial Download (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(100 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/facility-and-tribal-download-summary" target="_blank">Facility and Tribal Spatial Download Summary</a></td><td><span>Download of facilities nationwide that are located on or near (within 25 miles of) tribal land. Boundaries for both American Indian Reservations, American Indian Off-reservation Trust Lands, and Oklahoma Tribal Statistical Areas were collected from the U.S. Department of Commerce (USDOC), U.S. Bureau of the Census (Census Bureau). Originally reported by federally recognized tribal governments, these boundaries were updated&nbsp;by Census Bureau through the Boundary and Annexation Survey (BAS) on May 1, 2024 (American Indian Reservations) and April 15, 2024 (Alaska Native Villages, Off Reservation Trust Lands, and Oklahoma Tribal Statistical Areas) respectively.&nbsp;Virginia Federally Recognized Tribes contains point data for tribes geographically located in the state of Virginia, corresponding with the administrative boundaries of EPA Region 3.&nbsp;These tribes are federally recognized, but do not currently have land in federal satus. Locations are based on mailing addresses for each tribe provided by the EPA Region 3 Tribal Program Coordinator to the US EPA Office of Mission Support on May 5, 2021 and remain current as of April 15, 2025.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="air">Air Stationary Source Data Downloads</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/ICIS-AIR_downloads.zip">ICIS-Air Dataset (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(64 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-air-download-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-Air Download Summary</a></td><td>Data from EPA's Integrated Compliance Information System (ICIS) for Clean Air Act Stationary Sources.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/POLL_RPT_COMBINED_EMISSIONS.zip"><ins>Air&nbsp;Emissions Dataset (ZIP)</ins>&nbsp;</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(150 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/air-emissions-download-summary" target="_blank">Air Emissions Download Summary</a></td><td>Combined air emissions data for stationary sources from four EPA air programs: National Emissions Inventory (NEI), Greenhouse Gas Reporting Program (GHGRP), Toxics Release Inventory (TRI), and Clean Air Markets. Emissions are presented as facility-level aggregates and organized by pollutant and EPA program. For general information about these air programs, see <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/help/reports/air-pollutant-report-help" target="_blank">Air Pollutant Report Help</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/afs_downloads.zip">AFS Dataset (ZIP)</a><span class="fileinfo">(118 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/system/files/AFS_Data_Download.pdf" target="_blank">AFS Download Summary (PDF)</a><span class="fileinfo">(20 pp, 220 K, &nbsp;</span><a href="http://www.epa.gov/epahome/pdf.html" target="_blank"><span class="fileinfo">About PDF</span>&nbsp;</a><span class="fileinfo">)</span></td><td>Frozen data from EPA's retired Air Facility System (AFS) for Clean Air Act stationary sources. <span class="warning">ECHO Clean Air Act data from AFS are frozen and reflect data as of October 17, 2014.&nbsp;</span>(For information on the transition to ICIS-Air, see <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/resources/general-info/echo-faq/air-data-system" target="_blank">How New National Air Data System Affects ECHO Data Display</a>.)</td></tr><tr><td><span class="warning">New!</span><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/pipeline_caa_downloads.zip" title="CAA Pipeline Download (ZIP)">CAA Pipeline Dataset (ZIP)</a> (22 MB)</td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/caa-pipeline-download-summary" title="CAA Pipeline Download Summary">CAA Pipeline Download Summary</a></td><td><p>The Pipeline analysis of the Clean Air Act (CAA) data show the connection of each violation (identified by a violation activity id) to it's Compliance Monitoring Activities (CMA) and any Enforcement Actions (EA) linked to that violation activity identification value.</p><p>The download zip file includes:</p><ul><li>The Complete CAA Pipeline Dataset</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="NPDES">Water National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System (NPDES) Data Downloads</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page(s)</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_downloads.zip">ICIS-NPDES National Dataset (Part 1) (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(301 MB)</span></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="4"><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-download-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-NPDES Download Summary</a></td><td>Data from EPA's Integrated Compliance Information System (ICIS) for NPDES. Part 1 of the ICIS-NPDES national dataset. Due to its size, the national dataset is split into two files. Note that data for Master General Permits are provided in a separate file.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_eff_downloads.zip">ICIS-NPDES National Dataset (Part 2 - effluent violations) (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(2.5 GB)</span></td><td>Part 2 of the ICIS-NPDES national dataset. This file contains the data table for effluent violations.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-data-set" target="_blank">Effluent Violation Data by Jurisdiction</a></td><td>Link to download effluent violation data by a selected jurisdiction (e.g., state, territory, region).</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_master_general_permits.zip">NPDES Master General Permits (ZIP)</a> (96 K)</td><td>List of all versions of NPDES Master General Permits in ICIS-NPDES.&nbsp;A Master General Permit covers multiple facilities that have similar discharges and are located in a specific geographic area. A Master General Permit applies the same or similar conditions to all dischargers (also known as general permit covered facilities) covered by the permit.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_outfalls_layer.zip">ICIS-NPDES Discharge Points (ZIP)</a> (50 MB)</td><td colspan="1"><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-discharge-points-download-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-NPDES Discharge Points Summary</a></td><td>Location of facilities and permitted features (e.g., discharge points or outfalls) in ICIS-NPDES, with select facility, permit, and compliance data.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-dmr-and-limit-data-set" target="_blank">Permit Limit and DMR Data by Jurisdiction</a></td><td><p><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-limit-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-NPDES Permit Limit Summary</a></p><p><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-dmr-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-NPDES DMR Data Summary</a></p></td><td>Link to download ICIS-NPDES permit limit and Discharge Monitoring Report (DMR) data by a selected jurisdiction (e.g., state, territory, region).</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_limits.zip">National Permit Limit Dataset (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(459 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-limit-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-NPDES Permit Limit Summary</a></td><td>ICIS-NPDES national permit limit dataset for Clean Water Act permitted dischargers.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_prefy2009.zip">DMR Dataset for Years Prior To FY2009 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(1.3 GB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2009.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2009 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(240 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2010.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2010 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(254 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2011.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2011 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(270 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2012.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2012 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(288 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2013.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2013 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(312 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2014.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2014 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(385 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2015.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2015 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(409 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2016.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2016 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(474 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2017.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2017 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(531 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2018.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2018 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(547 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2019.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2019 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(461 MB)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2020.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2020 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(473 MB)</span><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2021.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2021 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(574 MB)</span><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2022.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2022 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(577 MB)</span><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2023.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2023 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;(596 MB)<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2024.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2024 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(612 MB)</span><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2025.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2025 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(565 MB)</span>&nbsp;<br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_dmrs_fy2026.zip">DMR Dataset for FY2026 (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(~100 MB)</span></td><td colspan="1"><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-npdes-dmr-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-NPDES DMR Data Summary</a></td><td colspan="1"><p>ICIS-NPDES national Discharge Monitoring Report (DMR) datasets by year for Clean Water Act permitted dischargers.</p><p>Note: The datasets for FY2010, FY2009, and years prior to FY2009 are refreshed monthly. All other DMR datasets are refreshed weekly.</p></td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/trends/loading-tool/get-data/monitoring-data-download">NPDES Monitoring Data Download</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br>Effluent Charts</td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/help/loading-tool/monitoring-data-download-help">NPDES Monitoring Data Download Help</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/help/reports/effluent-charts-help">Effluent Charts Help</a>&nbsp;and <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/help/tutorials#effluent">Effluent Charts Tutorial</a></td><td>View and download DMR data for one NPDES permit using either of these tools.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_attains_downloads.zip">NPDES Catchment Indexing and Assessed Waters Download (ZIP)</a> (66 MB)</td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/npdes-catchment-attains-summary" target="_blank">NPDES Catchment Indexing and Assessed Waters Summary</a></td><td>Spatially derived linkage between ICIS-NPDES and ATTAINS to associate surface water information (e.g., reach, catchment, waterbody impairment, etc.) to NPDES permittee locations.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="MSGP">Industrial Stormwater - Multi-Sector General Permit (MSGP)</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/aim_triggering_events_dl.zip">Additional Implementation Measures (AIM) Dataset (11/25/2025) (ZIP)</a> (62 K)</td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/msgp-aim-download-summary">Multi-Sector General Permit Additional Implementation Measures Data Download Summary</a></td><td>Link to download the most recent EPA Additional Implementation Measures (AIM) data.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="biosolids">Water Biosolids Data Download</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/npdes_biosolids_downloads.zip">ICIS-NPDES Biosolids Facility Dataset (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(764 KB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/biosolids-download-summary" target="_blank">ICIS-NPDES Biosolids Facility Data Download Summary</a></td><td>Facility and compliance information for NPDES permits in the ECHO Biosolids facility universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br>Biosolids data submitted electronically through NetBiosolids is available through the <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/facilities/facility-search?mediaSelected=bioAnnual" target="_blank">Biosolids Annual Report Search</a> and will be available for download through ECHO via a new dashboard (upcoming feature).</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="seweroverflow">Sewer Overflow Data Downloads</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/ALL_CSO_downloads.zip">All&nbsp;CSO downloads (ZIP)</a>&nbsp;<span class="fileinfo">(271 K)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/cso-inventory-summary" target="_blank">EPA's National Combined Sewer Overflow Inventory Summary</a></td><td>The National Combined Sewer Overflow Inventory was first published to ECHO in May 2023 to reflect the most current inventory of <a href="https://www.epa.gov/npdes/combined-sewer-overflows-csos">combined sewer overflow (CSO)</a> outfall locations across the United States. These data are updated weekly by EPA Regions and states, as described on <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/resources/echo-data/about-the-data#sources" target="_blank">About the Data</a>. Please also see the <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/resources/echo-data/known-data-problems">Known Data Problems</a> page for known data sharing issues that affect data completeness or accuracy for this national inventory. You can also use the <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/map-service">National Combined Sewer Overflow Inventory Service</a> to map these outfalls.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/current_sewer_overflow_and_collection_systems_tables.zip">Sewer Overflow and Bypass Event Dataset (ZIP)</a> (~516 KB)</td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/sewer-overflow-download-summary" target="_blank"><span>NPDES Sewer Overflow and Bypass Event Download Summary</span></a></td><td><p><span>Sewer overflow and bypass data collected under the NPDES Electronic Reporting rule (“NPDES eRule”). The report collects data on anticipated and unanticipated bypasses, wet-weather combined sewer overflows (CSOs) that “endanger the health or environment”, dry-weather discharged from CSOs, sanitary sewer overflows (SSOs) to the waters of the United States, and SSOs that are not in compliance with the standard NPDES permit requirements. This data download includes event details, relevant permit information, causes, corrective actions, impacts, affected waterbodies, type of event, and treatment equipment or plans.</span></p><p><span>The data are refreshed daily. The majority of data collection began in March 2025, and also includes historical events.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><span class="warning">New!</span><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/all_sewer_overflow_and_collection_systems_tables.zip">Sewer Overflow and Bypass Event All Versions Dataset (ZIP)</a> (~745 KB)</td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/sewer-overflow-all-versions-summary" target="_blank">All Versions Download Summary</a></td><td>This "all versions" dataset provides the full transaction history of data collected for sewer overflow and bypass events, while the NPDES Sewer Overflow and Bypass Event dataset provides the current version. This dataset was developed to track data entry updates and past versions of data submitted about overflow events.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="hazardouswaste">Hazardous Waste Data Download</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/rcra_downloads.zip">RCRAInfo Dataset (ZIP)</a><span class="fileinfo">(103 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/rcrainfo-download-summary" target="_blank">RCRAInfo Download Summary</a></td><td>Resource Conservation and Recovery Act compliance and enforcement data from EPA's RCRAInfo for hazardous waste sites.&nbsp;Additional RCRAInfo data are available on EPA's <a href="https://rcrapublic.epa.gov/rcrainfoweb/action/main-menu/view" target="_blank">RCRAInfo Web</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="warning">New!</span><br><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/pipeline_rcra_downloads.zip">RCRA Pipeline Dataset (ZIP)</a><span class="fileinfo">(~30 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/rcra-pipeline-download-summary" target="_blank">RCRA Pipeline Download Summary</a></td><td><p>The Pipeline analysis of the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (RCRA) data shows all Compliance Monitoring Activities (CMA) and identifies any violations and/or enforcement actions linked to those CMAs.</p><p>The download zip file includes:</p><ul><li>A Read me file which provides a summary of each included file.</li><li>The Complete RCRA Pipeline table. &nbsp;This is provided as a convenience, but does not contain an ISN_RCR_EVAL key. &nbsp;Therefore, it is the following three files which are &nbsp;most useful: RCRA Evaluations, RCRA Violations, and RCRA Enforcement Actions.</li><li>A RCRA Evaluations table with a generated ISN_RCR_EVAL key which can be used to link to their violations and enforcement actions.</li><li>A RCRA Violations table linked to evaluations by the ISN_RCR_EVAL key.</li><li>A RCRA Enforcement Actions table linked to evaluations by the ISN_RCR_EVAL key.</li></ul><p>The download file is updated weekly. &nbsp;The weekly run date is included as part of the ISN_RCR_EVAL key.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="ECM">EPA Enforcement and Compliance Monitoring Data Download</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/case_downloads.zip">ICIS FE&amp;C Dataset (ZIP)</a> <span class="fileinfo">(73 MB)</span></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/icis-fec-download-summary" target="_blank">ICIS FE&amp;C Download Summary</a></td><td>EPA data from EPA's Integrated Compliance Information System (ICIS) for federal compliance monitoring activity data not already included in the ICIS-Air and ICIS-NPDES downloads available above and federal&nbsp;civil enforcement action data. This includes federal compliance monitoring and enforcement data for programs not typically included in ECHO Facility Searches, such as CAA 112(r), non-NPDES CWA, EPCRA, FIFRA, RCRA Underground Storage Tanks, and TSCA.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="drinkingwater">Drinking Water Data Downloads</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/SDWA_latest_downloads.zip">SDWA Dataset (ZIP)</a> (457 MB)</td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/sdwa-download-summary" target="_blank">SDWA Data Download Summary</a></td><td>National download of Safe Drinking Water Act data compiled from the <a href="https://echo.epa.gov/resources/echo-data/about-the-data#sources" target="_blank">latest refresh</a> of Safe Drinking Water Information System (SDWIS) in ECHO. This dataset is updated quarterly.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="WQI">Water Quality Indicators (WQI) Data Download</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/files/echodownloads/Data-Analytics/WQI/" target="_blank">WQI Data Archive</a></td><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/maps/water-quality-indicators">WQI Homepage</a></td><td>Link to Water Quality Indicators (WQI) Background page.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="PFAS">National PFAS Data Downloads</h3><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Help Page</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://echo.epa.gov/tools/data-downloads/national-pfas-datasets" target="_self">National PFAS Datasets</a></td><td>N/A</td><td>Link to a collection of data downloads that can be used to evaluate what is known about per- and poly-fluoroalkyl substances&nbsp;(PFAS) reporting, testing, and occurrences in communities.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      
  </div>

</article>

